# Nightly ua-coins quote for the coins of the finished series
# (db_map.json's "completed" list -- NOT the whole NBU catalog).
#
# Install (as the deploy user, on the server):
#     mkdir -p ~/logs     # cron opens the log BEFORE the script runs,
#                         # so this one has to exist beforehand
#     docker compose --env-file ~/coinkeeper/.env \
#         -f ~/coin-parser/deploy/docker-compose.collector.yml build
#     crontab ~/coin-parser/deploy/crontab
#
# Times are the SERVER's local time, not UTC.
#     crontab -l          # check it took
#
# The server runs on UTC, and this cron (Ubuntu's vixie 3.0pl1) has no
# CRON_TZ -- the binary carries no timezone handling at all -- so the
# hour here has to be written in UTC by hand.
#
# 07:10 UTC is 10:10 in Kyiv while Ukraine is on EEST (UTC+3). It slips
# to 09:10 Kyiv when the clocks go back at the end of October; move this
# line to 08:10 then if the Kyiv hour is what matters. Nothing breaks
# either way -- load-prices reopens the last REFRESH_WINDOW_DAYS days to
# correction, so a quote read too early is fixed by a later history
# read rather than kept forever.
#
# Why not the old 03:15: ua-coins does not have the day's number that
# early. It recomputes during the morning (2026-09-10: still 349 at
# 08:13 UTC, 357 by 08:51), so a night run banked a figure the site
# itself had not settled on.
#
# The :10 rather than :00 is kept from the original: ua-coins rate-limits
# hard, and every scraper in the world fires at the top of the hour.
10 7 * * * /home/deploy/coin-parser/deploy/run-update-prices.sh >> /home/deploy/logs/update-prices.log 2>&1
